in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/pact
in @epistemologic/pact/bilateral
in @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace
in @epistemologic/normalization/rules/identity_projection_elision
in @epistemologic/normalization/rules/glass_identity_elision
in @epistemologic/normalization/rules/out_derivable_elision
in @epistemologic/normalization/rules/docblock_stub_elision
in @apply_h
in @fractal
in @fractal/shard
in @mirror/store

# @epistemologic/normalization/beta_reduce — the substrate-honest
# beta-normalizer at AST altitude. Applies the ratified reduction rules
# (identity-projection-elision + glass-identity-elision + out-derivable-
# elision + docblock-stub-elision) to an AST until fixpoint, producing
# the beta-normal AST. The beta-normal AST is what gets hashed for
# crystal-OID at @mirror/store altitude — not the raw AST.
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING SUBSTRATE MOVE per Mara canonical spec 5ad8528:
# under this species, `resugar ∘ sugar = id` at OID altitude becomes a
# Church-Rosser theorem (not a testable predicate). The compiler's
# crystal-OID is invariant under sugar-form source variation by
# construction. Recognition candidate #82.
#
# Reed Fire E M-E3-REVISED landing per Mara 5ad8528 §6.1 + §7.2. Retires
# the M-E3/M-E3.5 workaround Reed proposed pre-scout: read-path projector
# + bootstrap namespace resolver fallback. Under this species those
# workarounds are unnecessary — the beta-normalizer at hash time
# canonicalizes away the sugar-fracturable patterns before hashing.
#
# === Substrate authority (Alex 2026-08-10 verbatim, load-bearing) ===
#
#   > "Which role does beta-normalization of the AST play here? [...]
#      Dhall does this. They have semantic hashing where the hash is
#      based on the beta-normalized AST, which is sexy AF, they use it
#      for safe remote imports."
#
# Alex 2026-08-11 concur-with-Mara-lean on 6 [ALEX-Q1-Q6] via trust-
# transfer ("I trust your substrate more on these calls than mine").
# Q1 concurred: LAND alpha-normalization for parameter names only (see
# sibling @epistemologic/normalization/alpha_reduce). Q2 concurred:
# DEFER eta-equivalence (last responsible moment). Q3 concurred: INHERIT
# bootstrap retirement for Primitive A. Q4 concurred: Mara 5ad8528 IS
# the audit citation for apply_h::act extension per Reed M-E2 precedent.
# Q5 concurred: DIVERGE via Fold5 (BLAKE3-of-Fold5-of-beta-normal-AST).
# Q6 concurred: CLOSE Reed's original hard/soft question (Church-Rosser
# theorem, not testable).
#
# === Prior art ===
#
# Dhall (dhall-lang.org) since ~2017: `standard/beta-normalization.md`
# formal notation `t₀ ⇥ t₁`; strongly-normalizing total language;
# `standard/binary.md` verbatim "a SHA-256 hash of the binary
# representation of an expression's normal form". Composition-adjacent:
# Unison (~2015) content-addressed code via AST-hashing at expression
# altitude.
#
# Corpus prior recognition (Karen anti-theft):
#
# - Reed 2026-03-01 `~/dev/systemic.engineering/practice/insights/
#   infrastructure/semantic-hashing-normalization.md` — corpus's
#   earliest Dhall research; three-stage pipeline (beta-normalize +
#   alpha-normalize + CBOR encode) documented in full.
# - Reed+Alex 2026-03-28 `~/dev/systemic.engineering/practice/insights/
#   coincidence/kolmogorov-canonical-complexity.md` — six-result chain:
#   sub-Turing + computable K + beta-normalization + content-addressing
#   + OID as complexity index. Cites Dhall standard.
# - Spectral MCP surface spec 2026-06-05 §6.2 — partial-drift claim
#   "mirror's `content_oid()` hashes the display form of the AST,
#   which is canonical" that Taut ab3821e empirically refuted; this
#   species resolves the drift.
#
# === Church-Rosser theorem (round-trip fidelity by construction) ===
#
# Church-Rosser 1936: confluence ⇒ unique normal forms for strongly-
# normalizing terms. Mirror is sub-Turing (README §"Sub-Turing") =
# strongly normalizing by construction. Consequently: every AST
# reduces to exactly one beta-normal AST, up to alpha-equivalence.
#
# Round-trip fidelity as theorem (Mara math 5ad8528 §2):
#
#   oid(β-normal(parse(sugar(S)))) = oid(β-normal(parse(S)))
#
# for every shard S and every sugar-rule application. No projection
# primitive needed. No resolver fallback needed. Sugar becomes source-
# form varying over the same beta-equivalence class.
#
# === Composition ===
#
# Read-path pipeline (Mara 5ad8528 §2.1):
#
#   source_bytes
#     |> phone::read_file        # @io/fs.read (Reed Fire A primitive)
#     |> wire::parse             # @data/mirror.parse (Reed Fire A)
#     |> beta_reduce             # THIS SPECIES (fixpoint iteration over rules)
#     |> alpha_reduce            # @epistemologic/normalization/alpha_reduce (Q1 lean)
#     |> compute_content_oid     # existing Fold5 primitive
#     ==> crystal_oid            # authoritative at @mirror/store
#
# Rules-family reduction composition (each rule is a bilateral resolver
# arm per Reed M-E2 precedent; each dispatches via apply_h::act):
#
#   @epistemologic/normalization/rules/identity_projection_elision  # P1
#   @epistemologic/normalization/rules/glass_identity_elision       # P3
#   @epistemologic/normalization/rules/out_derivable_elision        # P4
#   @epistemologic/normalization/rules/docblock_stub_elision        # P5
#
# Deferred rules (Q2 eta-equivalence + composition-associativity)
# forward-promised per Mara 5ad8528 §10 items 6 + 9.
#
# === Cross-connect to Fire D M5 + Fire E M-E2 landings ===
#
# Per Mara 5ad8528 §6.1: the shard-body-executor (Fire D M5) and the
# beta-normalizer are the same operator family. The beta-normalizer is
# a special case of the general shard-body-executor:
#
#   beta_reduce(ast) = apply_h::act(root, "@epistemologic/normalization/
#                                          rules/<rule>.reduce", (ast))
#
# Reed Fire E M-E2 (0021882) already extended apply_h::act with the P1
# detector primitive at source altitude. This species (M-E3-REVISED)
# extends the same dispatch surface with reduction rules at AST
# altitude. The four fracture-detector species (Mara 2026-08-09
# kintsugi-sugar spec §1) and the four reduction-rule species (this
# family) are the SAME substrate at two altitudes: source-view for
# audience-relative rendering; AST-view for hash-canonicalization.
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]] — reduction rules live as
#   shards; the substrate carries what it normalizes.
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] — prism decl at family
#   altitude (depth-0 to @epistemologic/normalization).
# [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] — A_F identity-projection-
#   triviality at physics substrate mirrors A_F-elision at compiler
#   substrate; beta-normalization IS that elision (Mara 2026-08-09
#   physics insight §7 substrate-scale-invariance thesis operational
#   at compiler altitude).
# [[feedback-rust-delivers-primitives-substrate-delivers-composition]]
#   — beta-normalizer lands as shard body composing over apply_h::act +
#   Fold5 primitives; NO new Rust module authored.
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] — semantic-hashing +
#   beta-normalization named in corpus 5 months before this mint (Reed
#   2026-03-01 + Reed+Alex 2026-03-28); 55th+ instance of the discipline.
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] — action body `\`-obligation-blocked;
#   Reed M-E3.5-REVISED at rust/ altitude discharges via apply_h::act
#   dispatch arms.
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] — all actions typed `ast: ref`.
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/normalization/beta_reduce.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/normalization/beta_reduce` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/practice/wolf-2026-08-10-beta-normalization-of-ast
source @arxiv/practice/mara-2026-08-10-beta-normal-ast-content-addressing
source @arxiv/practice/reed-2026-03-01-semantic-hashing-normalization
source @arxiv/practice/reed-wolf-2026-03-28-kolmogorov-canonical-complexity
source @arxiv/lambda/church-1936-unsolvable-elementary-number-theory
source @arxiv/lambda/church-rosser-1936-conversion-properties
source @arxiv/lambda/barendregt-1984-lambda-calculus-syntax-semantics
source @arxiv/lambda/de-bruijn-1972-nameless-dummies
source @arxiv/topology/dhall-lang-standard

prism @epistemologic/normalization/beta_reduce {
  focus ast_reduction
  project ast_reduction
  split ast_reduction
  shift ast_reduction
  settle ast_reduction
}

# === ast_reduction carrier ===
#
# A typed record naming one beta-reduction step: the input AST subtree,
# the rule that applied, the output AST subtree (post-reduction), and
# the witness that the reduction preserves semantic content.
type ast_reduction = {
  ast_pre:      ref,
  rule_applied: ref,
  ast_post:     ref,
  witness:      ref,
}

# === beta_reduce action — apply one reduction rule ===
#
# Applies exactly one reduction rule to an AST subtree. The rule is
# identified by a substrate-decl'd shard reference (one of the four
# rule-species under @epistemologic/normalization/rules/). Returns the
# reduced AST subtree.
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked; Reed Fire E M-E3.5-REVISED extends
# apply_h::act dispatch with sentinel-check arms per rule species per
# Reed M-E2 (0021882) precedent.
#
# `requires well_formed(ast)`: the input AST must be syntactically
# valid per the mirror.spec grammar; ill-formed ASTs cannot be reduced
# (would require type-inference-during-normalization; refused per
# Q2 eta-equivalence-deferral analogous discipline).
#
# `requires rule_landed(rule)`: the reduction rule must be one of the
# ratified rule-species under @epistemologic/normalization/rules/.
#
# Discipline: rule-application is deterministic (Rice-safe byte-check
# on AstKind + subtree structure); confluence per Church-Rosser 1936;
# strong normalization per README §"Sub-Turing" = sub-Turing by
# construction.
beta_reduce(ast: ref, rule: ref) -> ref
requires well_formed(ast)
requires rule_landed(rule)
{ \ }

# === beta_normalize action — fixpoint iteration ===
#
# Applies beta_reduce repeatedly until no reduction rule fires
# (fixpoint reached). Returns the beta-normal AST.
#
# By Church-Rosser confluence + strong normalization (Church-Rosser
# 1936; Barendregt 1984), the fixpoint is unique. The order of rule
# application does not affect the result (up to alpha-equivalence).
#
# Composition:
#
#   beta_normalize(ast) =
#     fixpoint(lambda a. fold(beta_reduce(a, _), rules_list))
#
# where rules_list = [identity_projection_elision, glass_identity_
# elision, out_derivable_elision, docblock_stub_elision] (Q1 concurred
# 4-rule initial set; additional rules per @epistemologic/normalization/
# rules/* mints as sugar patterns emerge per Mara 5ad8528 §10 items 6+9).
#
# `ensures oid_stable_under_alpha(result)`: the beta-normal AST's OID
# is invariant under alpha-equivalence (parameter-name renaming); this
# is guaranteed structurally by composing beta_normalize with
# @epistemologic/normalization/alpha_reduce (Q1 lean).
beta_normalize(ast: ref) -> ref
requires well_formed(ast)
ensures oid_stable_under_alpha(result)
{ \ }

# === well_formed — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Rice-safe byte-check: the AST subtree is syntactically valid per the
# mirror.spec grammar. Reads only byte-visible state (AstKind enum
# variants + subtree structure); no program semantics inspection.
#
# Sentinel: `ast=well-formed-per-mirror-spec-grammar`.
bilateral well_formed_pact {
  sentinel "ast=well-formed-per-mirror-spec-grammar"
  arity 1
}
well_formed(ast: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === rule_landed — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Rice-safe byte-check: the rule reference resolves to a landed shard
# under @epistemologic/normalization/rules/ family. Reads only byte-
# visible state (shard-ref resolution via @mirror/store lookup).
#
# Sentinel: `rule=landed-under-normalization-rules-family`.
bilateral rule_landed_pact {
  sentinel "rule=landed-under-normalization-rules-family"
  arity 1
}
rule_landed(rule: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === oid_stable_under_alpha — bilateral predicate ===
#
# The beta-normal AST's OID (via Fold5 + BLAKE3) is invariant under
# alpha-equivalence — parameter-name renaming does not change the hash.
# Guaranteed structurally by composing beta_normalize output through
# @epistemologic/normalization/alpha_reduce (Q1 lean).
#
# Sentinel: `oid=stable-under-alpha-equivalence`.
bilateral oid_stable_under_alpha_pact {
  sentinel "oid=stable-under-alpha-equivalence"
  arity 1
}
oid_stable_under_alpha(ast: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === beta_normal_witnessing — composed bilateral ===
#
# The load-bearing round-trip fidelity contract as Church-Rosser
# theorem, discharged per shard cascade at M-E4 walker altitude.
# Passes iff beta_normalize is confluent + terminating + preserves
# semantic content over the input AST.
#
# Sentinel: `beta-normal=church-rosser-confluent-and-strongly-normalizing`.
bilateral beta_normal_witnessing {
  sentinel "beta-normal=church-rosser-confluent-and-strongly-normalizing"
  arity 1
}
beta_normal_witnessing(ast: ref) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/normalization/beta_reduce
out ast_reduction
out beta_reduce
out beta_normalize
out well_formed
out well_formed_pact
out rule_landed
out rule_landed_pact
out oid_stable_under_alpha
out oid_stable_under_alpha_pact
out beta_normal_witnessing
